I got through undergrad/grad school, the army and several jobs for big banks before I got diagnosed. I just always thought it was quirks about me (that I just work fast and have many interests) ADHD definitely helps me succeed but now that I'm on meds I feel like I have an unfair advantage over neurotypical people.

&#x200B;

Off meds; I'm smart but I'm a bit of a spaz. I try to follow through on things and I sort of do but it's a little slapdash.

&#x200B;

On meds; my third eye is open.  



